Hmm, wait, one subtle point: when both are the same kind of container, do we always recurse even if "containers" differ in structure? Yes: dict vs dict recurse on keys (keys only in one side become +/- with whole subtree value); list vs list recurse on indices (extra trailing items become +/-).

What about a dict vs dict where a's value is a scalar and b's value under the same key is a dict? → at that path recurse → not both same kind → `~` with whole value rendered. Good, matches test_list_of_dicts/test_type_change `~ $.a: [1] -> {"0": 1}`.

Also top level: a is dict, b is dict → recurse. a is dict, b is list → `~ $: ...`. a is scalar vs container → `~`.

